1. Modules
1.1 - main case
1.2 - rack handles
1.3 - foot switch

Project is optimise for MIDI purposes such as live performance optimisation and automation.
I design these models to integrate them with rack case and my system within the rack.
We can put our device to our rack case and control it using pedal switches or MIDI.
In earlier stage of this project i thought that its best to go with MIDI and encoder
minimalistic interface just to test presets since we put this in rack but then something remind me
of amp foot switches that are basically another control circuit. ant then i realise that we could do something
similar using attiny13a, 3 potentiometers, MIDI out and have fun with pure mechanical design.

getting to the point we will read 3 potentiometers and buttons with our attiny and send information via MIDI to
our main circuit. Our pedal will be printed with gear hatch with 5:1 ratio to potentiometer gear so when we turn
pedal form 0 to 35 degrees our potentiometer will turn from 0 to 175.

I will put here both .3mf and .f3d formats so you can already print or modify design as you wish.

